HST Office: ribbon commands show their icons.

A command's icon is used in a toolbar or the ribbon only when its UI command entry has the image
property (Properties bit 1): the module image manager registers only those commands. Six ribbon
commands have HST glyphs but no such entry, so they showed their text instead, and the text made
their groups wider (Writer's Font group carried "Xoay vòng kiểu chữ" at full length):
.uno:ChangeCaseRotateCase, .uno:InsertLabels, .uno:OriginalSize (GenericCommands), .uno:ClearContents
(CalcCommands), .uno:FormatDropcap, .uno:TextWrap (WriterCommands).

